# Replace MDEditor with Tiptap in AdminArticleForm

Replace the current MDEditor with Tiptap, a modern, lightweight rich text editor with better UX and features.

## Objective

Replace MDEditor in `src/pages/AdminArticleForm.js` with Tiptap while:
- Maintaining the current section-based layout (title, category, content sections)
- Adding proper table support
- Ensuring clean, production-ready code
- Removing all MDEditor bloat
- Keeping the same workflow (create/edit articles)

## Requirements

### 1. Install Tiptap Dependencies

Add these packages to `package.json`:
```json
{
  "@tiptap/react": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/starter-kit": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-image": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-table": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-table-row": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-table-header": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-table-cell": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-placeholder": "^2.1.13",
  "@tiptap/extension-link": "^2.1.13"
}
```

### 2. Remove MDEditor

**Remove:**
- `@uiw/react-md-editor` from package.json
- `@uiw/react-markdown-preview` from package.json
- Any MDEditor imports in `AdminArticleForm.js`
- MDEditor-specific CSS if any

### 3. Create Tiptap Editor Component

Create `src/components/TiptapEditor.js` and `src/components/TiptapEditor.css`:

**Features to include:**
- Rich text formatting (bold, italic, underline, strikethrough)
- Headings (H1, H2, H3)
- Lists (bullet, numbered)
- Tables (insert, add/remove rows/columns, merge cells)
- Links
- Images (with integration to existing image upload modal)
- Code blocks
- Blockquotes
- Horizontal rules
- Undo/redo
- Placeholder text

**Toolbar layout:**
- Text formatting buttons (B, I, U, S)
- Heading dropdown
- List buttons
- Table menu with dropdown
- Link button
- Image button (opens existing ImageUploader modal)
- Code block button
- Blockquote button
- Horizontal rule button
- Undo/redo buttons

